# Green Chile Mac

Based on [https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/…](https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/green-chile-mac/17021) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20230308094449/https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/green-chile-mac/17021/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1/2 tsp [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }, plus more as needed
- [ ] 8 oz [dried pasta shells]{ ing="dried-pasta-shells" } (medium-size)
- [ ] 1/4 cup [full-fat coconut milk]{ ing="full-fat-coconut-milk" } (see Note)
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [extra-virgin olive oil]{ ing="extra-virgin-olive-oil" }
- [ ] 2/3 cup [low-sodium vegetable broth]{ ing="low-sodium-vegetable-broth" }, or more as needed
- [ ] 1.5 tsp [Dijon mustard]{ ing="dijon-mustard" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [nutritional yeast]{ ing="nutritional-yeast" }
- [ ] 1 [garlic clove]{ ing="garlic-clove" }, quartered
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [onion powder]{ ing="onion-powder" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [Spanish smoked paprika]{ ing="spanish-smoked-paprika" } (pimentón), plus more for garnish
- [ ] 6 oz (1.5 cups) [frozen cubed butternut squash]{ ing="frozen-cubed-butternut-squash" }
- [ ] 2 oz (1/3 cup) roasted, salted [cashews]{ ing="cashews" }
- [ ] One 4-oz can diced [mild green chiles]{ ing="mild-green-chiles" }, drained
- [ ] [Ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }, for garnish

## Recipe

1. Boil pasta until al dente, according to package instructions, then drain
1. While the pasta cooks, make the ‘cheese’ sauce: Whisk together [coconut milk]{ ing="full-fat-coconut-milk" }, [oil]{ ing="extra-virgin-olive-oil" }, [broth]{ ing="low-sodium-vegetable-broth" }, [Dijon mustard]{ ing="dijon-mustard" }, [nutritional yeast]{ ing="nutritional-yeast" }, garlic, [onion powder]{ ing="onion-powder" }, [smoked paprika]{ ing="spanish-smoked-paprika" }, and the 1/2 tsp of [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } in a medium saucepan
1. Add the frozen [butternut squash]{ ing="frozen-cubed-butternut-squash" } and [cashews]{ ing="cashews" }. Cook over medium-low heat, barely bubbling at the edges, for 10 minutes
1. Transfer the sauce ingredients to a blender, add 3 Tbsp of the [green chiles]{ ing="mild-green-chiles" } and puree to form a smooth, cheesy-looking sauce. (A high-powered blender such as a Vitamix makes quick work of it; if using a standard blender, you may need to add a splash more [vegetable broth]{ ing="low-sodium-vegetable-broth" }). Taste, and add more [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } as needed
1. Return the drained pasta to the pot, then stir in the sauce and the remaining [green chiles]{ ing="mild-green-chiles" }
1. Serve with a garnish of [smoked paprika]{ ing="spanish-smoked-paprika" } and [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }

## Notes

1. Note: Thoroughly stir the coconut milk before using to re-incorporate its fat. You’ll use most of the remaining coconut milk from a 15-oz can in the Veggie-Loaded Red Curry
1. Week 3
